{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the word 'flesh' [בשר] is the body.</b> For it feels, but the substance does not feel. Now the covenant is that the body will not be cut off by the waters of the flood. And perhaps He included in the covenant that there will never again be a flood, so that they may be saved if a flood comes. And concerning this covenant it is said, 'as I swore that the waters of Noah would not pass over again' (Isaiah 54:9)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:55.264222775Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}